30,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings suggest a risk of instability. Supplier windows for certain tech are unreliable, and winter road closures can isolate parts of our network.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"It's sad, but some outer wards lost their bus links. However, the old outreach stops were actually more popular than the main building midweek!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"The funding structure is problematic. Grants only cover session fees for a year, and last year's vehicle running costs were significantly over budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"History repeats itself. A digitisation project from six years ago failed to index half its images, but partner-run evening groups are still thriving.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We have retired tradespeople who can help, but we have no one on the payroll trained to supervise outside facilitators. Also, our tool certification expert retired.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, if vehicle costs are overrunning, any proposal relying on a fleet might be a liability, especially with the road closures I found.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, but the people in those wards are stranded! We have to find a way to reach them, even if the roads are tricky.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I understand the need, but we cannot commit to a service that drains our operating budget after the first year of grant funding.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, that's why we should look at the partner-run model. My data shows those groups survived without constant internal funding.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, that sounds nice, but who will supervise them? I found that we lack the internal training to manage outside facilitators.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, that is a critical point. If we lack the skills to supervise, we are relying on conditions we cannot control.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, maybe the community can help? If the neighbourhood associations are already doing it, can't we just support them?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, support still requires a budget. If the grant expires and the operating budget is thin, the service will collapse.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, the evidence from six years ago shows that community-led groups are the only ones that actually last.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just don't want the current staff to be overwhelmed by things they aren't trained for.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We need a solution that is low-maintenance and doesn't depend on volatile supply chains or weather.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Yumi,,But it must be accessible. We can't ignore the people who lost their bus links.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,George,,It must be financially sustainable beyond the initial grant.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,May,,And it should be based on what has actually worked in this system before.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,It needs to fit the skills we actually have on the roster.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
